  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A uniform electric field of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is created between two parallel charged plates (as shown in figure). An electron enters the field symmetrically between the plates with a kinetic energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>eV</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The length of each plate is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>)</mo></math> of deviation of the path of electron as it comes out of the field is ______(in degree).</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/b0a2f662-96ce-4fec-af47-df9ffda86136-9894312.PNG\" style=\"width: 327px; height: 160px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "45",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/19d7b95b-6e55-4f63-a16c-f84194158a8a-9894312_1.PNG\" style=\"width: 319px; height: 160px;\" /></p><p>Given here, kinetic energy&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math></p><p>Acceleration of electron due to electric field is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></math>, where,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi></math>&nbsp;is charge on electron.</p><p>Using equation of motion,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp; along&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;direction, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8757;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mi>t</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Using equation of motion, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mi>t</mi></math>&nbsp;along y direction, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mi>t</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>From equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>, we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>tan</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mi>E</mi></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac><mfenced><mfrac><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>The angle of deviation of the path of electron as it comes out of the field is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p>",
